1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,919
Whether he's just taken one heck of a beating,

2
00:00:06,889 --> 00:00:17,019
or acting as meaty power armor for his bro, Jake the Dog is one hell of a powerhouse,

3
00:00:17,269 --> 00:00:18,620
when he wants to be at least.

4
00:00:19,059 --> 00:00:25,059
So today, we're gonna find out just how powerful he really is, starting with his 1% cursed Jake form,

5
00:00:25,399 --> 00:00:30,320
and steadily marching towards his final 100% empowered Starchild stage.

6
00:00:30,719 --> 00:00:35,579
At 1% power, come along with me and see Jake about as weak as he gets,

7
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:39,899
thanks to some nasty business with a witch in the episode, The Witch's Garden,

8
00:00:40,159 --> 00:00:41,600
after he steals from a donut garden.

9
00:00:42,039 --> 00:00:43,119
Yeah, I think so.

10
00:00:43,299 --> 00:00:47,240
Whoa! What did she do to you?

11
00:00:47,539 --> 00:00:49,840
I stripped him of his magical powers.

12
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:52,259
For stealing one of your billions of donuts?

13
00:00:52,579 --> 00:00:55,000
Yeah, it's not like I killed your husband or something.

14
00:00:55,119 --> 00:00:56,439
I am not married!

15
00:00:56,780 --> 00:01:00,560
Getting all your magic stripped away for stealing donuts seems pretty unfair.

16
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:03,240
At least she gave him underwear to go with those human legs.

17
00:01:03,579 --> 00:01:08,780
You'll be unsurprised to learn, Jake minus all his powers, is an exactly hero tier.

18
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,099
See, Jake's a doer, not a thinker.

19
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:16,439
When Finn and Jake do go and try to get his powers back, he almost immediately doinks it up.

20
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:18,120
Yeah, let's do it!

21
00:01:18,299 --> 00:01:19,640
Oh my gosh!

22
00:01:20,450 --> 00:01:23,640
I forgot that I don't have magic powers anymore.

23
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,140
How do we search for the mud without my powers?

24
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:26,920
We run!

25
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:28,959
Run like energetic little boys!

26
00:01:29,319 --> 00:01:33,260
This whole time, I thought running was some sort of leg magic.

27
00:01:34,670 --> 00:01:35,739
Look at me!

28
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:37,560
I'm running!

29
00:01:38,019 --> 00:01:43,560
Less than 10 seconds into an adventure, and the dog is already taking a nasty beating from the unmoving ground.

30
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:48,640
The 1 mile per hour jog isn't exactly impressive either, but we'll give him some slack.

31
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:52,540
Those legs are new, and he did just fall like 20 feet.

32
00:01:52,959 --> 00:01:58,040
He probably can be blamed for listening to his subconscious and quickly getting as lazy as possible,

33
00:01:58,519 --> 00:01:59,879
though. You're right, Jake.

34
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:00,989
It is exhausting.

35
00:02:01,579 --> 00:02:02,420
What are you?

36
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:03,930
I'm your subconscious!

37
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:06,200
Okay, what are you doing here?

38
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:09,199
I'm here to tell you that what you're feeling deep down inside is true.

39
00:02:09,539 --> 00:02:11,860
It is way too hard to swim across the river.

40
00:02:12,139 --> 00:02:13,280
It's easier to wear a hat.

41
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:14,280
Here, have a hat!

42
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,879
Yeah! Jake!

43
00:02:18,199 --> 00:02:19,199
Stop talking to yourself!

44
00:02:19,319 --> 00:02:20,300
Cross over already!

45
00:02:20,599 --> 00:02:24,639
Yeah, it's probably time to move on from a non-magical baby-legged Jake.

46
00:02:25,159 --> 00:02:28,539
Spoiler, but he stays about this lazy the whole episode,

47
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:33,219
and he isn't going to shock you with many feats of strength until he gets his powers back.

48
00:02:33,419 --> 00:02:37,599
Honestly, the only impressive thing he does while cursed is trick the witch into fixing him.

49
00:02:37,819 --> 00:02:38,580
Not like that.

50
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:40,020
Our boy is a father.

51
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:41,810
Alright, I think you've learned your lesson.

52
00:02:42,020 --> 00:02:42,840
I forget you.

53
00:02:43,270 --> 00:02:44,680
My powers!

54
00:02:44,979 --> 00:02:46,659
How can I ever think- Ha!

55
00:02:46,819 --> 00:02:47,439
Gotcha, Kane!

56
00:02:51,810 --> 00:02:54,460
But didn't you learn your lesson?!

57
00:02:54,460 --> 00:03:00,939
Nope! Even weakened and incredibly lazy, Jake is always ready for a good cheap shot.

58
00:03:01,159 --> 00:03:02,500
Crocodile Tears for the win!

59
00:03:02,719 --> 00:03:05,599
I don't blame you if 1% Jake didn't knock your socks off,

60
00:03:05,759 --> 00:03:09,400
but now let's see what good old 8% Jake is capable of.

61
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:13,259
At 8% power, take a gander at our plucky hero at his baseline.

62
00:03:13,879 --> 00:03:16,560
Even at this stage, Jake is good at handing out whoopins,

63
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,740
but he's definitely not pushing himself.

64
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,699
We'll see peak Jake later.

65
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,560
We see the epitome of 8% Jake in the episode Who Would Win,

66
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:26,939
where he and Finn fight a legendary foe.

67
00:03:27,159 --> 00:03:31,639
One who accepts any and all challengers, and seems to think of himself as invincible.

68
00:03:32,039 --> 00:03:35,659
The moment Finn sees this dude, he knows he's gotta fight him.

69
00:03:35,939 --> 00:03:36,979
What's going on here, tough boy?

70
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:38,560
What is that huge dude?

71
00:03:39,099 --> 00:03:41,919
He's the farm, the legendary fighter of the Shiny Isles.

72
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:46,120
I came here to participate in his open challenge, but this mother can't be beat.

73
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:47,500
Give up, worms!

74
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:49,639
My fight power is supreme!

75
00:03:50,099 --> 00:03:52,659
I'm too freakin' legendary!

76
00:03:57,889 --> 00:04:00,080
The farm is one tough cookie.

77
00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:04,180
Jake isn't super into it when the idea of fighting the dude is pitched,

78
00:04:04,379 --> 00:04:07,180
but we're gonna get to see him flex his fighting spirit regardless.

79
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:09,439
Just... one minor issue?

80
00:04:09,759 --> 00:04:13,560
Finn gets mad peeved when he wants to train to prepare for their big match,

81
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:15,759
and Jake phones it in super hard.

82
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:20,529
After breaking Jake's copy of the game Compies Castle, there's a bit of an escalation.

83
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:25,100
And by that, I mean Jake really tries to beat the tar out of his friend.

84
00:04:25,399 --> 00:04:26,279
Hi-ya!

85
00:04:26,839 --> 00:04:36,040
COMPIE! I'm gonna break every bone in your body,

86
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:40,680
then heal you later with that magical goo we got from the Cyclops' eye!

87
00:04:41,540 --> 00:04:42,920
Aaaaah! Ouch!

88
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:46,680
Apologize! Never!

89
00:04:47,259 --> 00:04:52,899
Delivering some brotherly threats is one thing, but Jake is quickly going to prove he really means what he says.

90
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:56,160
Those were the eyes of a dog off the deep end.

91
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:58,939
Dang, this is really gonna get nasty, huh?

92
00:05:06,129 --> 00:05:07,800
This isn't how you train.

93
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:10,040
Maybe Finn started it, but now what?

94
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:13,759
The only one who looks like he can really hurt Jake in this fight is Jake.

95
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,680
It's not like Finn is gonna whip out a sword against his brother.

96
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:17,620
Where are ya?

97
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:20,439
Huh? Apologize for not taking training seriously!

98
00:05:21,519 --> 00:05:23,579
Come out, you chicken nung!

99
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:26,660
Ow! Ow!

100
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:29,839
Just compare the pain the two are dealing out.

101
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:34,939
Finn might deal the occasional jab in this fight, but Jake is gonna send his brother to the hospital!

102
00:05:35,300 --> 00:05:37,079
Pretty soon, Finn gets himself stuck.

103
00:05:37,319 --> 00:05:42,100
Unfortunately, Jake's a huge problem, often metaphorically and literally,

104
00:05:42,420 --> 00:05:43,699
when you've got nowhere to go.

105
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:54,100
Apologize to Copy's castle!

106
00:05:54,259 --> 00:05:57,560
No, you apologize for not taking training seriously!

107
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:02,300
That was at least 23 kicks, by the way.

108
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:05,339
This fight is honestly one of the more brutal in the show,

109
00:06:05,620 --> 00:06:07,139
and it's between two best friends.

110
00:06:07,620 --> 00:06:10,540
Maybe seeing two pals fight is biasing me, actually.

111
00:06:10,759 --> 00:06:13,819
I guess the pair do literally kill monsters in some way.

112
00:06:15,279 --> 00:06:19,980
чи rings me, it's a hospital time and bolts in that gone.

113
00:06:31,139 --> 00:06:35,699
So, Jake is a magical dog and maybe could handle that kind of damage,

114
00:06:35,879 --> 00:06:39,839
but Finn definitely almost died if not for his squishy bro, right?

115
00:06:39,860 --> 00:06:43,600
right? Neither party is doing great after that fall, obviously,

116
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:49,160
but I hope I look half as good if I ever fall down a ravine and am crushed by trees.

117
00:06:49,399 --> 00:06:51,730
I mean, I also really hope that never happens,

118
00:06:52,199 --> 00:06:53,879
but that's besides the point.

119
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:58,870
After their fight, Ven and Jake have the interesting idea to try to beat the farm individually.

120
00:06:59,379 --> 00:07:00,399
Hey, come on!

121
00:07:00,579 --> 00:07:01,680
You gotta fight the dude!

122
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:04,240
I can't see!

123
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:05,279
Walk me to the light!

124
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:06,540
Yeah, that's what you get!

125
00:07:16,110 --> 00:07:18,519
Loud looks like a car.

126
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:19,980
Cool plan.

127
00:07:20,300 --> 00:07:22,620
Really showing off what good fighters you are, bros.

128
00:07:22,879 --> 00:07:24,620
Thankfully, the pair are at least tenacious.

129
00:07:25,839 --> 00:07:28,639
After getting some advice in a dream and patching up their friendship,

130
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:32,800
they come up with a plan that isn't suicide with extra steps.

131
00:07:47,149 --> 00:07:48,240
Gotta give it to them.

132
00:07:48,759 --> 00:07:51,079
Not many would bite an ass to achieve victory,

133
00:07:51,339 --> 00:07:53,220
but that's what makes a true hero.

134
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:54,399
Or something.

135
00:07:54,699 --> 00:07:57,019
Now, for all his claims about his power,

136
00:07:57,180 --> 00:08:01,459
the farm wasn't too tough once the pair gave it their all and remembered to fight his pals.

137
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:08,579
So, what happens when our favorite hero actually needs to give his doggy all rather than his normie 8% power?

138
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:09,819
Well, I'll call that one.

139
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:14,360
Try Hard Jake and boost his rating all the way up to 13% power.

140
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:16,120
He got that dog in him now.

141
00:08:16,759 --> 00:08:18,199
You may need to sit down for this,

142
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:21,259
but Jake doesn't try very hard most days.

143
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:23,339
Unless he's playing card games, I guess.

144
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:26,879
However, he will, on occasion, get some fire in his heart.

145
00:08:27,339 --> 00:08:30,379
We see this in a couple episodes, including Blade of Grass,

146
00:08:30,579 --> 00:08:34,700
which basically cold cuts to Jake already showing some real power and talent.

147
00:08:47,879 --> 00:08:48,779
Thanks, bro.

148
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:52,299
You notice that playtime was over once he felt Finn was in trouble?

149
00:08:52,779 --> 00:08:55,000
That's the power of love and violence, baby.

150
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:58,409
Blade of Grass is probably one of Finn's most important episodes,

151
00:08:58,740 --> 00:09:01,240
but Finn ain't Jake, so we gotta move on.

152
00:09:01,620 --> 00:09:06,980
Let's now cut to The Limit, an episode all about Jake pushing to the very limit of his powers.

153
00:09:07,620 --> 00:09:12,740
After realizing he and Finn can't cheat to get through a maze, they're looking for some lost hot dogs,

154
00:09:13,279 --> 00:09:14,480
Jake comes up with a plan.

155
00:09:14,860 --> 00:09:18,340
Then, I'll just hook my legs around this stump and stretch us through so we don't get lost.

156
00:09:18,460 --> 00:09:19,000
Like this, see?

157
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:20,940
Haha, you're a cool guy, Jake.

158
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:21,740
Thank you.

159
00:09:22,179 --> 00:09:24,259
How far can our doggy actually go?

160
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:26,039
Not even he really knows.

161
00:09:26,379 --> 00:09:28,919
Unfortunately, he sure starts thinking about that later,

162
00:09:29,379 --> 00:09:32,700
when he needs to fight after stretching like crazy to explore the maze.

163
00:09:32,899 --> 00:09:35,539
Oh, and the lost hot dogs have also been found.

164
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:37,200
Fresh hazards!

165
00:09:38,110 --> 00:09:39,320
Grab him up, Jake!

166
00:09:40,539 --> 00:09:41,799
Flex him!

167
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:44,539
I can't stretch anymore!

168
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,200
You can do it, Jake!

169
00:09:46,539 --> 00:09:47,899
Stretch, stretch, stretch!

170
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:51,700
All this stretching really starts to make me think about Jake's guts.

171
00:09:52,059 --> 00:09:55,759
It can't feel good to be messing with all your insides that much.

172
00:09:56,019 --> 00:10:01,559
Ugh. But whether he should or not, this magic dog can indeed stretch even more.

173
00:10:07,279 --> 00:10:08,679
Jake! Come on, baby!

174
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:13,940
Jake! Jake!

175
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:17,580
Jake! Gollum, taken care of.

176
00:10:18,019 --> 00:10:21,450
Wow, Jake trying his hardest is upsetting.

177
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:27,259
That dog don't look so good, and it's like purely because he's stretched so thin.

178
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:34,200
Yet, like any true hero facing the terrible enemies of peer pressure and trying to impress strangers, he struggles on.

179
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:37,639
Surely he will experience no consequences from this.

180
00:10:38,059 --> 00:10:40,179
Boop, boop, boop, boop, boop, boop, boop, boop, boop, boop.

181
00:10:40,179 --> 00:10:41,019
Ha ha ha ha!

182
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:42,000
Stop, man!

183
00:10:42,340 --> 00:10:42,740
Ha ha ha!

184
00:10:43,399 --> 00:10:43,799
Foo hoo hoo!

185
00:10:44,279 --> 00:10:46,340
No! Oh!

186
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:47,960
Oh my god!

187
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:49,340
It's okay!

188
00:10:49,919 --> 00:10:52,059
Hot dogs are immune to poison!

189
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:54,220
Sick! I got it!

190
00:10:58,370 --> 00:11:01,399
Hey, so I know chocolate is poisonous to dogs,

191
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:06,799
but I also think tons of venomous scorpion stings are also poisonous to dogs, right?

192
00:11:07,159 --> 00:11:08,659
I'll have to ask my vet.

193
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:12,500
I guess Jake can still talk, so let's just see how he's feeling.

194
00:11:12,860 --> 00:11:13,580
I'm good, man.

195
00:11:13,759 --> 00:11:15,879
It's the small scorpions you gotta worry about.

196
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,039
Or is that just with snakes?

197
00:11:17,799 --> 00:11:19,259
Nope. Wait.

198
00:11:19,539 --> 00:11:20,779
Poison's kicking in.

199
00:11:20,940 --> 00:11:23,559
You might wonder if any of this is worth it.

200
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:25,080
I sure would.

201
00:11:25,299 --> 00:11:28,600
But apparently you can get a wish if you get to the end of this maze,

202
00:11:29,159 --> 00:11:32,679
which is a pretty good deal if you don't get your dog killed on the way.

203
00:11:32,879 --> 00:11:35,039
Hmm. So how is Jake?

204
00:11:35,059 --> 00:11:39,620
Jake, after even more miles of stretching and with a gallon or two of poison flowing in him.

205
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:41,259
You think you can stretch up there, buddy?

206
00:11:41,919 --> 00:11:42,899
Yes! Oh!

207
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:44,120
Jake, you okay?

208
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:45,220
Uh, yeah.

209
00:11:45,419 --> 00:11:47,120
I just can't close my eyes.

210
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:47,779
Okay, dude.

211
00:11:47,919 --> 00:11:48,659
This is too far.

212
00:11:48,899 --> 00:11:49,539
No more maze.

213
00:11:49,679 --> 00:11:50,200
We're going home.

214
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:52,200
Yeah, I'm feeling a little thin.

215
00:11:52,799 --> 00:11:55,740
This is as impressive as it is sad.

216
00:11:56,100 --> 00:11:58,299
And that's not even the end.

217
00:11:58,580 --> 00:12:00,679
The hot dogs convince him to go further.

218
00:12:01,100 --> 00:12:04,419
Even Finn gets in on the toxic peer pressure game eventually.

219
00:12:04,860 --> 00:12:05,419
Jake! Jake!

220
00:12:05,419 --> 00:12:06,480
Jake! Jake!

221
00:12:06,659 --> 00:12:07,240
Jake! Jake!

222
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:07,759
Jake! Jake!

223
00:12:07,759 --> 00:12:10,620
Yeah! Jake!

224
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:11,820
Yeah! Jake!

225
00:12:11,820 --> 00:12:13,539
Yeah! That's it.

226
00:12:13,679 --> 00:12:14,080
I'm dead.

227
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:16,899
Jake! Stay with me, man.

228
00:12:17,019 --> 00:12:19,059
Meh. But we did it, okay?

229
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:21,039
I can wish you out of here, man.

230
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:21,919
See, kids?

231
00:12:22,179 --> 00:12:26,460
You too can earn wishes by exploiting your friends and pushing them to the brink of death.

232
00:12:26,740 --> 00:12:29,289
So then, Finn wishes for Jake to...

233
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:33,460
what? Oh, he wishes for a cool psychic war elephant.

234
00:12:33,799 --> 00:12:34,919
But hold on a second.

235
00:12:35,639 --> 00:12:36,259
There's a plan.

236
00:12:36,539 --> 00:12:38,419
Now wish for my friends to be healed.

237
00:12:38,559 --> 00:12:41,940
I wish for what Finn desires.

238
00:12:42,799 --> 00:12:43,860
Yeah, boy!

239
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:47,059
No! You weren't supposed to have your wishes come true.

240
00:12:47,379 --> 00:12:48,600
You were supposed to die.

241
00:12:48,899 --> 00:12:50,259
Now bust us out of here.

242
00:12:50,590 --> 00:12:52,460
No! Yeah, boy!

243
00:12:53,740 --> 00:13:00,740
I guess the lesson is that it's okay to give in to extremely dangerous peer pressure as long as somebody

244
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:03,200
then undoes all the bad consequences of your actions.

245
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:05,320
Hmm, I may want to call my lawyer.

246
00:13:05,539 --> 00:13:10,379
Whatever. Tryhard Jake is just barely 13% of what this doggy can do.

247
00:13:10,679 --> 00:13:15,879
So let's move on to 24% of Jake's maximum potential, Ice Ninja Jake.

248
00:13:16,429 --> 00:13:18,809
Yeah, so it doesn't come up a lot.

249
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:24,259
But one time, Jake learned a bunch of ice powers in the episode, The Chamber of Frozen Blades.

250
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:29,940
This is all thanks to a book they find when snooping around Ice King's castle called Ninjas of the Ice,

251
00:13:30,259 --> 00:13:31,740
The Art of Fridjitsu.

252
00:13:32,019 --> 00:13:34,899
That's frigid plus ninjitsu for all you non-masters.

253
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:37,840
I ain't even heard of these techniques.

254
00:13:41,139 --> 00:13:44,179
Some of the powers are pretty basic.

255
00:13:44,679 --> 00:13:46,639
It's cool and all that Jake can make ice weapons,

256
00:13:46,980 --> 00:13:49,899
but our boy can grow giant and hit like a semi-truck already.

257
00:13:50,179 --> 00:13:54,860
It's a bit more impressive when he shows off his ability to summon ice arrows and other weapons.

258
00:13:55,299 --> 00:13:57,159
Because at least that's a ranged attack.

259
00:13:57,639 --> 00:14:00,960
Fridjitsu master Finn summons dagger of chilled glass.

260
00:14:01,360 --> 00:14:05,879
Fridjitsu master Jake summons stars of frozen rain.

261
00:14:06,399 --> 00:14:08,169
Get ready to be starstruck.

262
00:14:08,460 --> 00:14:10,460
Get ready to be cold cut.

263
00:14:10,919 --> 00:14:16,980
Frankly, I'm starstruck enough to almost look past how cringe a white kid and his dog pretending to be ninjas is.

264
00:14:17,379 --> 00:14:18,259
I'll even admit it.

265
00:14:18,460 --> 00:14:20,440
They are doing real ice ninja moves.

266
00:14:20,980 --> 00:14:24,000
Maybe they got legit ninja potential and I'm just a hater.

267
00:14:26,879 --> 00:14:28,879
Kunai attack!

268
00:14:29,799 --> 00:14:31,899
Icicle kick!

269
00:14:32,940 --> 00:14:34,659
Force of blizzard!

270
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:37,139
Flying jump!

271
00:14:38,179 --> 00:14:39,419
Yeah, you know what?

272
00:14:39,779 --> 00:14:44,039
I don't think you count as a wannabe if you're throwing out attacks and dodging like that.

273
00:14:44,259 --> 00:14:48,940
Also, wow, I would be peeved at all the stuff they're breaking if I was Ice King.

274
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:52,220
Thank goodness they're not going to destroy even more stuff.

275
00:14:53,019 --> 00:14:53,299
What's that?

276
00:14:53,519 --> 00:14:54,039
I see.

277
00:14:54,379 --> 00:14:55,200
Three jigs?

278
00:14:55,399 --> 00:14:56,500
That's one too many.

279
00:14:56,820 --> 00:14:57,779
Caltroth Nailstorm!

280
00:15:00,009 --> 00:15:01,759
Those jigs were all fakes!

281
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:06,379
Heh! Fridjitsu master Jake summons arrow of ice!

282
00:15:08,639 --> 00:15:12,799
I know the bros are just playing here, unlike that stuff with the farm,

283
00:15:13,259 --> 00:15:14,399
but uh...

284
00:15:14,399 --> 00:15:19,700
I don't think launching sharp ice over and over at family is a good idea,

285
00:15:20,159 --> 00:15:22,159
even if you know they're professional heroes.

286
00:15:22,580 --> 00:15:27,659
At least they're not going all out, but then the Ice King comes back and things get serious.

287
00:15:28,279 --> 00:15:30,639
This enclosure will be your new home.

288
00:15:30,919 --> 00:15:31,860
He's got a princess!

289
00:15:32,299 --> 00:15:34,379
Now we leap out, catch him red-handed.

290
00:15:34,659 --> 00:15:35,860
Hey! Snow blind!

291
00:15:36,139 --> 00:15:38,100
That ice, that ice, that ice!

292
00:15:39,279 --> 00:15:42,730
But once you get used to the smell of penguin manure, it's almost tolerable.

293
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:45,320
Ice King!

294
00:15:45,519 --> 00:15:46,740
Hand over that princess!

295
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:48,639
Yeah! Princess?

296
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:49,919
What? Jake!

297
00:15:50,460 --> 00:15:51,120
Where's the princess?

298
00:15:51,580 --> 00:15:52,279
Ooh, right.

299
00:15:52,559 --> 00:15:56,860
I know stealth powers aren't always as cool as Goku going Super Saiyan or whatever,

300
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:01,059
but imagine a giant dog just appearing out of thin air behind you.

301
00:16:01,340 --> 00:16:02,419
I just give up.

302
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:08,200
But dang, how are we going to see these powers in action if the Ice King didn't actually abduct anyone?

303
00:16:10,039 --> 00:16:10,820
Oh no no no no!

304
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:11,279
Not that!

305
00:16:11,379 --> 00:16:11,779
Never mind!

306
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:14,840
Put that down and go clean my gym equipment.

307
00:16:17,539 --> 00:16:18,600
Dr. Princess!

308
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:22,639
Oh. Yeah, Ice King has once again earned a whooping.

309
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:25,340
Luckily, two heroes were around to give it to him.

310
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:26,379
How's your egg doing?

311
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:28,980
Oh! Oh!

312
00:16:31,519 --> 00:16:34,559
A lot of that whooping is admittedly off-screen.

313
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:38,360
Lame! At least we get to see the miracle of life in action.

314
00:16:38,620 --> 00:16:43,059
Also, yes, that was a kitten hatching from a penguin egg.

315
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:46,190
Well, he's not really a penguin, but whatever.

316
00:16:46,879 --> 00:16:48,759
So, who wins the actual fight?

317
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:53,100
Well, literal seconds later, you get your pretty obvious answer.

318
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:55,799
Gunter! Why didn't you tell me?

319
00:16:56,970 --> 00:16:58,500
Oh, Gunter!

320
00:16:58,879 --> 00:17:04,039
I'd seriously be worried kicking an old man like that would kill him.

321
00:17:04,279 --> 00:17:05,640
But it doesn't, so it's all good.

322
00:17:05,839 --> 00:17:13,279
Alright, let's jump from Jake's rare 24% ninja form to one of Jake's weirdest form in the whole dang show.

323
00:17:13,559 --> 00:17:20,160
At 41% power, watch Jake and his brother become a single dangerous and kinda gross powerhouse.

324
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:26,960
So, any real Adventure Time fan probably knows about the Jake suit, which is introduced in the episode, uh,

325
00:17:27,460 --> 00:17:27,900
Jake suit.

326
00:17:28,240 --> 00:17:32,200
This is when Finn wears Jake-like armor as a sort of brotherly fusion.

327
00:17:32,460 --> 00:17:38,619
While I rate it at about 41% power, its ickiness deserves at least a 75%.

328
00:17:41,779 --> 00:17:43,440
Yep! Yeah!

329
00:17:43,579 --> 00:17:44,819
Totally stuck to head landing!

330
00:17:45,039 --> 00:17:45,759
Yeah! Woo!

331
00:17:45,920 --> 00:17:46,579
Woo! Woo!

332
00:17:46,599 --> 00:17:49,180
Man, it's been so long since I've worn the Jake suit.

333
00:17:49,299 --> 00:17:50,299
I forgot how awesome it was.

334
00:17:50,339 --> 00:17:51,140
I know when your bot is, bro.

335
00:17:51,220 --> 00:17:52,099
Stretchy arm power!

336
00:17:52,380 --> 00:17:56,079
I feel unstoppable!

337
00:17:56,599 --> 00:17:59,319
Is it cheating to count this form when power scaling Jake?

338
00:17:59,640 --> 00:18:03,720
It's Jake doing the hard work, so I say we're all good.

339
00:18:04,099 --> 00:18:08,019
You also might guess that this form is a little tougher on Jake than his bro.

340
00:18:09,079 --> 00:18:10,680
Rawr! Damn!

341
00:18:11,259 --> 00:18:12,319
I don't even feel it!

342
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:15,140
Hmph! Beemo, throw your plate at me!

343
00:18:15,339 --> 00:18:16,380
Okay! Yeah!

344
00:18:16,460 --> 00:18:17,599
Yeah, Beemo, show me this stuff!

345
00:18:17,799 --> 00:18:18,259
Keep it coming!

346
00:18:18,519 --> 00:18:20,240
Yuck! Yeah, Beemo, at least the big!

347
00:18:21,470 --> 00:18:22,640
Unleash the beast!

348
00:18:22,940 --> 00:18:22,940
Unleash the beast!

349
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:27,119
These brothers really need to learn about setting healthy boundaries.

350
00:18:27,519 --> 00:18:32,299
Still, Finn ignoring his pals' comfort does help to show how tough Jake is.

351
00:18:32,599 --> 00:18:37,440
I also think we might be lucky Jake's skeleton clearly doesn't work like a normal dog's.

352
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:41,099
Especially when Beemo really starts to test things.

353
00:18:42,119 --> 00:18:46,000
You okay, Beemo?

354
00:18:46,019 --> 00:18:47,200
Are you okay, Beemo?

355
00:18:47,380 --> 00:18:49,200
I'm no match for the Jake suit.

356
00:18:49,539 --> 00:18:50,140
That's right!

357
00:18:54,299 --> 00:18:56,680
Dog, the Jake suit is mad strong!

358
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,579
Everybody needs to chill out!

359
00:18:58,900 --> 00:19:02,380
It's cool seeing how tough, agile, and strong our boy is,

360
00:19:02,460 --> 00:19:05,220
but Finn and Beemo really messed Jake up this episode.

361
00:19:05,440 --> 00:19:06,640
At least that's it.

362
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:10,920
Definitely. Nothing way worse happens seconds later, that's for sure.

363
00:19:11,509 --> 00:19:12,940
Sorta. Wait, bro.

364
00:19:13,140 --> 00:19:14,000
What are you doing up here?

365
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:16,240
You know I'm not with actual armor, right?

366
00:19:16,380 --> 00:19:17,440
Sam, top of the flame off the tree!

367
00:19:17,680 --> 00:19:19,059
Aaaaaaah! Noooooooooooooooo!

368
00:19:19,119 --> 00:19:20,640
Poing! Radom cowboy!

369
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:22,920
Wooo! Aaaaaah!

370
00:19:23,559 --> 00:19:24,880
Aaaaaah! Aaaaaah!

371
00:19:24,900 --> 00:19:25,380
Aaaaaah! Aaaaaah!

372
00:19:25,380 --> 00:19:30,500
Baaaaah! Look, the Jake suit form is great and all, but Jake is lucky he already had kids.

373
00:19:30,819 --> 00:19:34,619
I had like an actual physical reaction to seeing that fence thing.

374
00:19:35,019 --> 00:19:36,920
Eventually Jake stands up for himself a little,

375
00:19:37,220 --> 00:19:39,900
so we don't see the Jake suit until later in that episode.

376
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:44,420
Once we do, I feel like I just gotta ask, how hot is lava?

377
00:19:47,220 --> 00:19:57,380
I mean, they lived, guys.

378
00:19:57,880 --> 00:19:59,980
I don't really know what to say to that.

379
00:20:00,099 --> 00:20:00,920
It's insane.

380
00:20:01,299 --> 00:20:04,359
That wasn't like a blast of fire or a splash of lava.

381
00:20:05,019 --> 00:20:06,539
It was literally a volcano.

382
00:20:07,119 --> 00:20:08,210
I wouldn't be in the hospital.

383
00:20:08,619 --> 00:20:10,019
I'd just be missing.

384
00:20:10,460 --> 00:20:13,160
Should Jake be mad that Finn assumed they'd survive that?

385
00:20:13,519 --> 00:20:13,900
For sure.

386
00:20:14,160 --> 00:20:15,200
But they did survive.

387
00:20:15,839 --> 00:20:19,019
Which proves the Jake suit has earned its place on the power scale.

388
00:20:19,319 --> 00:20:21,579
In fact, Jake, and his human bro,

389
00:20:22,079 --> 00:20:28,440
surviving seemingly certain death kind of hints at a fact about Jake that the show only dives into very late.

390
00:20:28,859 --> 00:20:31,640
Jake the dog is at least 50% alien.

391
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:35,299
We shift now, much like a secretly alien half-dog,

392
00:20:35,740 --> 00:20:40,000
from our boy's 41% power Jake suit form, to his 77% alien.

393
00:20:40,079 --> 00:20:42,279
6% power star child form.

394
00:20:42,839 --> 00:20:43,380
That's right.

395
00:20:44,099 --> 00:20:45,900
Let's talk about Jake the star child.

396
00:20:46,259 --> 00:20:50,579
To give the 411, Jake's birth was, um, a little gross.

397
00:20:51,140 --> 00:20:54,140
And not like normal miracle of life gross.

398
00:20:54,680 --> 00:20:57,960
Jake first learns the truth in the episode, The First Investigation.

399
00:20:58,359 --> 00:21:03,099
Due to some time nonsense, he gets a peek at his parents, having a less than ideal time.

400
00:21:03,299 --> 00:21:06,839
Dad? So, I can see you, and you can see me.

401
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,700
And we're occupying the same space now.

402
00:21:08,900 --> 00:21:10,680
So this time stuff must be getting more intense.

403
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:15,619
Whoa! Hey, creeper, stop creeping on baby Jake!

404
00:21:17,500 --> 00:21:17,900
Baby Jake?

405
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:23,720
Yeah, in case you don't know, that ain't how the average dog is born.

406
00:21:24,039 --> 00:21:27,700
Jake's mom, Margaret, isn't biologically related to him.

407
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:31,880
Basically, a creepy alien put an egg in his dad's head.

408
00:21:32,019 --> 00:21:33,279
Biologically, our boy's mom is a creeper.

409
00:21:33,559 --> 00:21:35,420
Baby Jake is 50% Joshua the dog,

410
00:21:35,779 --> 00:21:38,960
and 50% Warren Ampersand, the shapeshifting alien.

411
00:21:39,220 --> 00:21:41,299
Margaret is just his stepmom who stepped up.

412
00:21:44,119 --> 00:21:45,460
Oh boy, our first case.

413
00:21:45,859 --> 00:21:47,059
Looks like we have a poltergeist.

414
00:21:48,690 --> 00:21:50,000
And it's got a little crush on me.

415
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:50,700
What a sassafras.

416
00:21:51,119 --> 00:21:51,920
Gotta get this on tape.

417
00:21:52,779 --> 00:21:54,740
You'll probably be unsurprised to learn,

418
00:21:54,779 --> 00:21:59,440
an alien that injects eggs into unwilling hosts and then abandons them is bad news.

419
00:21:59,759 --> 00:22:02,140
But we'll actually get back to Warren later.

420
00:22:02,539 --> 00:22:05,200
For now, that moment where Warren turns Jake blue,

421
00:22:05,500 --> 00:22:08,900
if you watch the show chronologically, it's going to look familiar.

422
00:22:09,380 --> 00:22:14,519
You see, in part 8 of the Elements arc, Skyhooks 2, gosh I sound like a nerd saying all that,

423
00:22:14,799 --> 00:22:20,240
Lumpy Space Princess saves the day by undoing the elemental magic that donked everyone up in that arc.

424
00:22:20,380 --> 00:22:22,940
But this power also made Jake look different.

425
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:25,619
Thank you, Starkey.

426
00:22:29,579 --> 00:22:30,480
Wait, where?

427
00:22:30,920 --> 00:22:31,460
Up here.

428
00:22:33,140 --> 00:22:34,619
You really donked up.

429
00:22:36,339 --> 00:22:38,099
Finn! Jake?

430
00:22:38,799 --> 00:22:41,160
Finn! Oh my gosh!

431
00:22:42,099 --> 00:22:42,519
Come here!

432
00:22:43,440 --> 00:22:45,539
What? Over here!

433
00:22:45,819 --> 00:22:46,640
Hey, buddy!

434
00:22:47,079 --> 00:22:48,480
Jake? Are you okay?

435
00:22:48,799 --> 00:22:51,960
Yeah. You know, everything looks different after a long trip.

436
00:22:52,420 --> 00:22:53,880
You and I can fix whatever this is together.

437
00:22:54,400 --> 00:22:55,700
Whenever. Fix what now?

438
00:22:55,859 --> 00:22:58,299
Yeah, the brothers don't realize it at that time.

439
00:22:58,759 --> 00:23:00,960
But that's Jake's star child form.

440
00:23:01,220 --> 00:23:08,279
He's still our boy, but LSP saving the day accidentally made Jake a little more like his absentee parent Warren the Alien.

441
00:23:08,619 --> 00:23:14,440
The next episode, Abstract, is really the one where we realize Jake doesn't just look different.

442
00:23:15,019 --> 00:23:19,259
While coming to terms with his new body, he also learns he has alien powers.

443
00:23:21,059 --> 00:23:22,599
So, how's your toast?

444
00:23:23,420 --> 00:23:23,819
Pretty good.

445
00:23:25,119 --> 00:23:28,420
Funny though, I can kind of taste the toast's emotions or something.

446
00:23:28,980 --> 00:23:33,099
Getting ground into flour and then made into bread really did a number on his wheat sense itself.

447
00:23:33,420 --> 00:23:36,819
Tasting the emotions of your food isn't exactly going to win you any battles,

448
00:23:37,220 --> 00:23:38,759
but it's definitely new.

449
00:23:39,240 --> 00:23:44,079
Star child Jake is, as literally everyone who sees him can tell, a little weird.

450
00:23:44,539 --> 00:23:49,039
A ton of this episode just covers Jake trying to accept this new alien version of himself.

451
00:23:49,480 --> 00:23:51,140
Dear, oh dear, that's really something.

452
00:23:51,579 --> 00:23:53,799
You know, I think I figured out why I make people uneasy.

453
00:23:54,220 --> 00:23:55,400
They're used to yellow Jake.

454
00:23:55,619 --> 00:23:56,759
Jackie, I'll get to the end.

455
00:24:13,769 --> 00:24:18,400
He's even naturally resistant to magic that would help him look more like the old Jake.

456
00:24:18,680 --> 00:24:23,380
He's still basically the same guy, but in a totally different, more powerful bod.

457
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:27,680
Star child Jake never learns everything his new form can do,

458
00:24:27,960 --> 00:24:29,000
so we don't either.

459
00:24:29,279 --> 00:24:35,519
In fact, this episode mostly dives into the fact that he's not as cool with his alien body as he wants to be.

460
00:24:35,660 --> 00:24:36,579
Same old Jake.

461
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:38,180
Completely normal.

462
00:24:40,910 --> 00:24:44,059
This looks bad, but deep down, I'm not different.

463
00:24:44,319 --> 00:24:45,740
And you're not different either, right?

464
00:24:46,039 --> 00:24:47,319
You'll go back to painting landscapes.

465
00:24:47,680 --> 00:24:49,220
No one is making me do this.

466
00:24:49,680 --> 00:24:54,480
I painted so many landscapes that the shapes of the land began to lose their meaning.

467
00:24:54,980 --> 00:25:00,460
Confronting how he's changed, thanks to the help of the often forgotten third brother of Finn and Jake, Jermaine,

468
00:25:00,779 --> 00:25:03,740
really helps our star child become a bit more zen.

469
00:25:04,039 --> 00:25:06,900
It also gives him some much needed control.

470
00:25:07,400 --> 00:25:10,799
Even if we're not changing on the outside, we're changing on the inside constantly.

471
00:25:11,299 --> 00:25:13,980
There's some stuff about me that I've been ignoring for a long time.

472
00:25:14,220 --> 00:25:16,579
I'm afraid of that stuff, but it's part of who I am.

473
00:25:16,839 --> 00:25:19,319
As long as I know the shape of my soul, I'll be alright.

474
00:25:21,420 --> 00:25:23,799
Wow, you really understand my art.

475
00:25:24,039 --> 00:25:25,900
Oh, I totally don't understand anything.

476
00:25:27,980 --> 00:25:29,759
That's some monk-level business.

477
00:25:30,240 --> 00:25:32,440
Jake turning yellow again also isn't a metaphor.

478
00:25:33,160 --> 00:25:37,940
He literally gains the ability to look like his old self by accepting his new self.

479
00:25:38,359 --> 00:25:43,220
Of course, if you're like me, you kind of wish we saw more of Jake's alien powers actually getting used.

480
00:25:43,619 --> 00:25:49,819
So let's cheat real quick and see something Jake might be able to do by peeking at his absentee bio-pop.

481
00:25:50,140 --> 00:25:51,880
Yeah, uh, Jake's around here somewhere.

482
00:25:52,039 --> 00:25:54,140
Popped right out of my dad's head for some reason.

483
00:25:54,339 --> 00:25:56,400
Man, it's crazy to think I was born here.

484
00:25:56,779 --> 00:25:58,559
Yeah! You scared me there.

485
00:25:58,660 --> 00:26:00,200
Now you're just reaching towards me.

486
00:26:01,859 --> 00:26:02,579
Let's go, son.

487
00:26:03,930 --> 00:26:06,119
I ain't nobody's son but Joshua and Margaret.

488
00:26:06,339 --> 00:26:09,259
Well, it is weird that you got exactly the same stretchy power as me.

489
00:26:09,400 --> 00:26:15,859
Warren can do all sorts of nonsense, but one of the more interesting things he can do is create portals.

490
00:26:16,319 --> 00:26:20,400
If Jake were more experimental, he might be able to do the same.

491
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:25,880
Although it definitely tires Warren out, and Jake does hate exerting himself.

492
00:26:26,099 --> 00:26:29,700
Hence the 76% power rating of his star child form.

493
00:26:30,099 --> 00:26:35,359
But now we gotta cut back to a very non-zen Jake form from much earlier.

494
00:26:35,660 --> 00:26:38,019
Brace your keister for a party nor'easter.

495
00:26:38,440 --> 00:26:42,400
We're going to a 92% power Jake, party animal Jake.

496
00:26:42,859 --> 00:26:45,380
Big time Adventure Time fans knew this was coming,

497
00:26:45,779 --> 00:26:49,440
but Jake was literally once imbued with godlike power.

498
00:26:49,779 --> 00:26:55,019
To make a long story a little shorter, it all starts when his brother was abducted by some strange characters.

499
00:26:55,660 --> 00:26:57,759
Untie me so I can beat you with that sack!

500
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:01,980
You're that- Yes, the charismatic stranger from last night!

501
00:27:02,319 --> 00:27:04,099
The grandmaster of the gnomes!

502
00:27:04,480 --> 00:27:06,539
Ruler of the Banithaverse!

503
00:27:07,740 --> 00:27:08,420
Pretty nice!

504
00:27:08,640 --> 00:27:13,400
Hey, why don't you guys just untie me and we can pretend this whole thing didn't happen!

505
00:27:13,839 --> 00:27:16,779
Those gnomes do not, in fact, let Finn go.

506
00:27:17,019 --> 00:27:21,019
Luckily, Jake eventually realizes something is wrong and looks for him.

507
00:27:21,299 --> 00:27:26,079
Eventually. His journey to godhood doesn't exactly start with a bang.

508
00:27:26,599 --> 00:27:30,140
Finn! Man, where is that kid?

509
00:27:30,380 --> 00:27:31,500
He's starting to worry.

510
00:27:31,779 --> 00:27:33,119
Take my sandwich, BMO!

511
00:27:33,220 --> 00:27:34,259
I'm gonna go find Finn!

512
00:27:34,509 --> 00:27:34,980
I'm gonna go find Finn!

513
00:27:34,980 --> 00:27:35,720
I didn't think, Bog!

514
00:27:35,920 --> 00:27:37,099
He gets distracted.

515
00:27:37,420 --> 00:27:38,460
Like, a lot.

516
00:27:38,920 --> 00:27:43,440
Most of this episode is watching Jake get sidetracked and Finn get tortured by gnomes, actually.

517
00:27:43,759 --> 00:27:51,599
However, Jake's lollygagging eventually pays off when he goes to a sick sky party featuring some water babes and someone a little special.

518
00:27:52,400 --> 00:27:56,299
So we brought you to the Cloud Kingdom with the Party God.

519
00:27:56,799 --> 00:27:59,059
Whoa! Who's the Party God?

520
00:27:59,299 --> 00:28:00,859
I am the Party God!

521
00:28:01,079 --> 00:28:05,839
You have won my favor for being a completely off-the-hook party dog!

522
00:28:06,410 --> 00:28:07,980
Woohoo! Ha ha ha!

523
00:28:08,259 --> 00:28:09,799
Yeah, that's not just a title.

524
00:28:10,140 --> 00:28:13,819
That floating wolf head with the hat is literally the God of partying.

525
00:28:14,019 --> 00:28:16,319
The Party God can honestly be kind of a tool.

526
00:28:16,660 --> 00:28:18,039
There's like a whole episode on it.

527
00:28:18,240 --> 00:28:20,299
But he thinks Jake is pretty dang rad.

528
00:28:20,680 --> 00:28:25,329
Because your gut waves please me so, I will grant you one wish.

529
00:28:25,819 --> 00:28:27,279
What do I want most?

530
00:28:27,460 --> 00:28:29,519
What do I want most in the world?

531
00:28:29,619 --> 00:28:32,380
I wish Finn would stop leaving his dirty- FIN!

532
00:28:33,200 --> 00:28:35,160
It's also nice that Jake does care about Finn.

533
00:28:35,559 --> 00:28:38,140
He's just also got that goldfish attention span.

534
00:28:38,339 --> 00:28:39,960
So, what does he wish for?

535
00:28:40,220 --> 00:28:42,079
Well, perhaps averting expectations.

536
00:28:42,240 --> 00:28:43,839
His wish is pretty simple.

537
00:28:44,019 --> 00:28:47,500
Party God, I wish that I could focus on fighting my friend Finn!

538
00:28:47,740 --> 00:28:49,759
Then your wish is mine.

539
00:28:50,079 --> 00:28:51,779
Wait! Is there some kind of catch?

540
00:28:52,769 --> 00:28:54,500
Yes, you got me.

541
00:28:54,680 --> 00:28:59,579
Man, was the Party God just gonna grant that wish genie style with no warning?

542
00:28:59,960 --> 00:29:02,700
Well, Jake at least caught him and gets a warning.

543
00:29:03,059 --> 00:29:06,180
Turns out a simple wish isn't necessarily simple to grant.

544
00:29:06,519 --> 00:29:10,460
Gang, I smell a temporary ultra power-up we'll never see again coming!

545
00:29:10,980 --> 00:29:12,980
One that drives our boy kinda nutso!

546
00:29:13,759 --> 00:29:19,140
To grant your wish, I will have to fill you with the energy of a thousand partying demons.

547
00:29:19,480 --> 00:29:24,339
You will become so overloaded with party energy that you'll demolish everything.

548
00:29:24,609 --> 00:29:26,059
in your path!

549
00:29:26,480 --> 00:29:30,660
So, how do we think Jake might handle…what was it?

550
00:29:31,019 --> 00:29:32,880
The energy of a thousand partying demons?

551
00:29:33,339 --> 00:29:33,960
Easy peasy.

552
00:29:34,359 --> 00:29:37,480
I'm sure that won't have any unexpected consequences whatsoever.

553
00:29:38,500 --> 00:29:39,319
None. At.

554
00:29:40,099 --> 00:29:42,839
All. Party!

555
00:29:44,099 --> 00:29:47,640
Party! I'm gonna shake it!

556
00:29:47,980 --> 00:29:50,500
Fire the shooting gun ray!

557
00:29:50,779 --> 00:29:51,740
High five!

558
00:29:52,140 --> 00:29:53,380
Freeze! Let!

559
00:29:53,680 --> 00:29:54,220
Catch her!

560
00:29:54,359 --> 00:29:55,319
Jake, buddy.

561
00:29:55,759 --> 00:29:58,480
I think you've got a little too much pep in your step.

562
00:29:58,720 --> 00:30:02,289
Well, at least he uses it to teach those gnomes a serious lesson.

563
00:30:02,579 --> 00:30:06,980
But how ever will Jake stop the gnome's ultimate planet twisting weapon?

564
00:30:07,259 --> 00:30:10,220
Haha! I meant I could lift this thing!

565
00:30:10,619 --> 00:30:22,059
So, I guess the power of a thousand partying demons plus one Jake the dog is enough to lift almost anything.

566
00:30:22,440 --> 00:30:27,220
Sure, the machine broke first, but… I think Jake could've done it if the thing didn't explode.

567
00:30:27,559 --> 00:30:29,220
But, like even the best parties,

568
00:30:29,619 --> 00:30:35,059
this form was but a fleeting moment of beauty and a frankly cocaine-esque energy.

569
00:30:35,460 --> 00:30:38,220
Jake! You defeated the gnomes!

570
00:30:38,279 --> 00:30:38,880
Yeah, man!

571
00:30:39,119 --> 00:30:39,740
You're okay?

572
00:30:40,099 --> 00:30:40,720
Yeah, man!

573
00:30:40,980 --> 00:30:41,500
I'm fine!

574
00:30:41,740 --> 00:30:42,519
Then I did it!

575
00:30:42,619 --> 00:30:45,599
I saved you by being an unfocused rowdy party dog!

576
00:30:45,839 --> 00:30:46,759
Haha! Yeah, dog!

577
00:30:47,019 --> 00:30:49,240
Yeah! Let's go eat cinnamon bun!

578
00:30:49,619 --> 00:30:54,039
With Finn saved and Jake's wish fulfilled, we won't see party animal Jake again.

579
00:30:54,359 --> 00:30:55,400
Maybe for the best.

580
00:30:55,640 --> 00:31:00,079
That level of power and that chaotic of a dog could probably destroy the world.

581
00:31:00,359 --> 00:31:09,619
You may be surprised to learn Jake has a form I place even above the insane 92% strength demon-powered pup you just saw.

582
00:31:09,799 --> 00:31:14,680
It was brief, it was beautiful, and it was in the episode Jake the Starchild.

583
00:31:14,940 --> 00:31:18,720
Prepare for Jake at 100% power!

584
00:31:19,039 --> 00:31:20,180
Also, I didn't goof.

585
00:31:20,440 --> 00:31:23,180
This is different from Baseline Starchild, I promise.

586
00:31:23,880 --> 00:31:29,339
Assuming you can remember what I talked about, like, five minutes ago, you'll recall the name Warren Ampersand,

587
00:31:29,759 --> 00:31:31,299
Jake's alien absentee parent.

588
00:31:31,720 --> 00:31:37,200
It's in the episode Jake the Starchild, where we finally get some major lore about Jake being half alien,

589
00:31:37,519 --> 00:31:40,200
after Warren takes Jake to a faraway planet.

590
00:31:41,279 --> 00:31:42,079
It's not weird!

591
00:31:42,319 --> 00:31:43,039
We have to leave!

592
00:31:43,299 --> 00:31:44,700
Right now!

593
00:31:45,099 --> 00:31:49,269
This is when Jake learns the specifics of what the show is hinting at for a while.

594
00:31:49,539 --> 00:31:51,859
Warren had shown up a couple times before this,

595
00:31:52,160 --> 00:31:54,900
but usually as just some mysterious stalker.

596
00:31:55,440 --> 00:31:59,940
You might rightfully ask how this is different from the Starchild stuff I already talked about.

597
00:32:00,440 --> 00:32:06,720
We'll get to that, starting with the fact that Warren spends some time pretending he doesn't suck and explaining a few things.

598
00:32:07,140 --> 00:32:08,819
There's also some guilt tripping.

599
00:32:09,259 --> 00:32:10,819
My name is Warren Ampersand.

600
00:32:11,200 --> 00:32:13,099
I'm your alien bio dad.

601
00:32:13,539 --> 00:32:14,559
Why do you keep laughing?

602
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:15,579
I'm nervous.

603
00:32:17,910 --> 00:32:20,220
Welcome to your home planet.

604
00:32:20,539 --> 00:32:25,940
Warren claims he's dying, and that Jake has an important role he needs to fill on Warren's home planet.

605
00:32:26,240 --> 00:32:28,440
He does a lot to gas up his son, too.

606
00:32:28,779 --> 00:32:32,059
Almost like there might be some alternate motives at play.

607
00:32:32,319 --> 00:32:33,720
Will you sign my prophecy book?

608
00:32:33,819 --> 00:32:35,319
Well, it feels so right, you know?

609
00:32:35,460 --> 00:32:37,519
Hey! It's my fifth birthday party!

610
00:32:37,700 --> 00:32:38,299
And my graduation?

611
00:32:38,839 --> 00:32:40,359
No, I don't remember this one.

612
00:32:40,579 --> 00:32:43,359
That's an artist's interpretation of the great prophecy.

613
00:32:43,740 --> 00:32:48,819
So, long story short, Warren abducts his son after years as an absentee father,

614
00:32:49,259 --> 00:32:52,460
and is apparently getting Jake to win some big, important fight.

615
00:32:52,680 --> 00:32:55,339
Spoiler, but none of that is real.

616
00:32:55,519 --> 00:33:00,480
Well, he is an absentee bio dad who is asking a big favor of a son who doesn't know him,

617
00:33:00,700 --> 00:33:04,259
but the first big step of the real plan starts soon after.

618
00:33:04,519 --> 00:33:07,500
I've researched your world and created the ideal child room.

619
00:33:07,819 --> 00:33:08,920
See? Space stop.

620
00:33:09,279 --> 00:33:10,779
Dinosaurs. And cowboys.

621
00:33:11,519 --> 00:33:12,759
Is that clown cake for me?

622
00:33:13,140 --> 00:33:14,740
I got you something else, too.

623
00:33:16,200 --> 00:33:19,180
Cool belts.

624
00:33:19,579 --> 00:33:21,460
Maybe you wish your own pops would get you one, huh?

625
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:23,559
Yeah, well, maybe not.

626
00:33:23,859 --> 00:33:27,920
Because those belts drain the power from whoever wears the one Jake has on,

627
00:33:28,240 --> 00:33:31,180
and gives that power to the wearer of the proud pop belt.

628
00:33:31,859 --> 00:33:35,059
Jake doesn't know that at first, but it's gonna matter soon.

629
00:33:35,359 --> 00:33:36,819
You might even see where this is going.

630
00:33:37,019 --> 00:33:38,599
Or you've watched this episode.

631
00:33:38,819 --> 00:33:40,039
Either way, let me build.

632
00:33:40,180 --> 00:33:42,720
See, Warren just can't keep his yapper shut.

633
00:33:44,190 --> 00:33:47,299
Yay, he's saving the galaxy's exhausting.

634
00:33:47,920 --> 00:33:48,279
I'm dying.

635
00:33:49,700 --> 00:33:55,480
With the seed of doubt planted by that accidental spy work, we shall soon get to see Jake's ultimate form.

636
00:33:55,720 --> 00:33:58,980
First, though, Jake needs to fully understand who Warren is.

637
00:33:59,240 --> 00:34:00,079
Like, for real.

638
00:34:00,440 --> 00:34:05,059
He finally gets it when fighting that monster Warren talked about goes a little...

639
00:34:05,059 --> 00:34:07,380
odd. Dude, weren't you, like, dying?

640
00:34:07,740 --> 00:34:08,400
Shush, son!

641
00:34:08,739 --> 00:34:09,900
Ish-chan-o approacheth!

642
00:34:11,739 --> 00:34:13,519
Whoa! I'll go grab the panzark.

643
00:34:15,019 --> 00:34:16,139
Stretch, baby!

644
00:34:16,480 --> 00:34:17,940
Stretch! Here comes the hero!

645
00:34:21,559 --> 00:34:22,739
You're doing it!

646
00:34:22,920 --> 00:34:24,019
God, this is too much!

647
00:34:24,300 --> 00:34:29,579
Yeah, so you may have noticed that, um, like,

648
00:34:29,639 --> 00:34:33,880
the whole planet turned off after Jake shot that thing and then pooped himself off?

649
00:34:34,199 --> 00:34:36,860
Even the machine he fired melted into the ground.

650
00:34:37,260 --> 00:34:43,219
Warren might be the worst dad of all time, but he also has almost got like, stretching power.

651
00:34:43,760 --> 00:34:49,099
Jake! What's going on?

652
00:34:49,340 --> 00:34:50,360
I have a confession.

653
00:34:50,699 --> 00:34:51,719
There's no Ish-chan-o.

654
00:34:51,880 --> 00:34:52,800
I made it all up.

655
00:34:53,099 --> 00:34:54,039
You're not really dying?

656
00:34:54,300 --> 00:34:55,800
No! I was dying!

657
00:34:56,039 --> 00:34:58,280
I needed to siphon your precious stretchy essence.

658
00:34:58,539 --> 00:35:01,840
I've done it hundreds of times to keep me young and virile.

659
00:35:02,059 --> 00:35:03,340
To hundreds of sons.

660
00:35:04,099 --> 00:35:06,219
The more you stretch, the stronger I grow.

661
00:35:06,579 --> 00:35:09,699
So, this explanation lets us know something pretty important.

662
00:35:10,099 --> 00:35:14,840
Warren is, at the very least, probably as strong as, like, hundreds of Jake's.

663
00:35:15,139 --> 00:35:17,500
He also doesn't have any daughters, I guess?

664
00:35:17,980 --> 00:35:22,179
After learning Warren actually kind of likes him, not enough not to kill him,

665
00:35:22,460 --> 00:35:25,679
but still, Jake comes up with a classic Jake plan.

666
00:35:26,199 --> 00:35:26,869
Pretend to be sad!

667
00:35:27,420 --> 00:35:29,159
But I never felt guilty before.

668
00:35:29,400 --> 00:35:34,079
Maybe it's this feeling your kind calls low-key affection?

669
00:35:34,800 --> 00:35:36,599
I'm sorry, Dad.

670
00:35:36,960 --> 00:35:39,460
I wasn't powerful enough to destroy Ish-chan-o.

671
00:35:39,639 --> 00:35:41,559
It was just me stretching the whole time.

672
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:43,900
You just say that to make me feel better.

673
00:35:44,179 --> 00:35:44,820
I'll prove it.

674
00:35:46,039 --> 00:35:46,800
I'm Finn!

675
00:35:47,280 --> 00:35:48,780
So, a few things.

676
00:35:49,139 --> 00:35:51,980
First, that hug is gonna matter, like, a minute later.

677
00:35:52,380 --> 00:35:57,579
Second, the draining belts mostly work when the guy being drained is using his stretchy powers.

678
00:35:58,079 --> 00:36:00,980
You're probably putting the pieces together now.

679
00:36:01,380 --> 00:36:07,639
Jake spends some time pretending his dad's transformations are cheering him up about the whole being murdered by his parasite father thing.

680
00:36:08,239 --> 00:36:13,320
For you see, Jake may easily be distracted and not so smart about a lot of things,

681
00:36:13,579 --> 00:36:15,460
but he's the king of cons.

682
00:36:16,139 --> 00:36:17,219
And here's Joshua.

683
00:36:17,500 --> 00:36:18,019
Do more.

684
00:36:18,380 --> 00:36:20,860
I'm no Warren Amphisan, but I guess I raised you.

685
00:36:21,119 --> 00:36:22,260
Here's a bunch of party bears.

686
00:36:22,360 --> 00:36:23,380
Make more party bears.

687
00:36:23,619 --> 00:36:25,199
Put party bears on the treehouse.

688
00:36:25,380 --> 00:36:26,900
Put party bears in the sky.

689
00:36:28,639 --> 00:36:32,800
Realizing he's in a corner, Warren then runs off after learning about Jake's pups.

690
00:36:33,099 --> 00:36:37,280
He's gonna go try and drain their stretchy powers if he can't get Jake's.

691
00:36:37,539 --> 00:36:46,519
But that just means Warren manages to peeve off Jake bad right after he got what's probably the biggest power boost of his puppy life.

692
00:36:46,980 --> 00:36:49,599
Old-fashioned grifting, you rube.

693
00:36:49,719 --> 00:36:50,739
I'm the proud pup.

694
00:36:50,920 --> 00:36:52,739
The belt totally applies to me as well.

695
00:36:53,059 --> 00:36:54,719
My real dad taught me that trick.

696
00:36:54,900 --> 00:36:56,230
But I was a proud pup.

697
00:36:56,480 --> 00:36:57,099
Five stretchy pups.

698
00:36:58,320 --> 00:36:59,840
You saved me after all.

699
00:36:59,980 --> 00:37:04,159
So, first, catching a rocket racing into space on its own is impressive.

700
00:37:04,659 --> 00:37:10,440
It's a small rocket, but if you told me to catch a missile or something, I think you'd be disappointed.

701
00:37:10,900 --> 00:37:12,639
But whatever you think about that,

702
00:37:13,019 --> 00:37:19,340
how much force do you think it takes to throw something through space while also avoiding the pull of a black hole?

703
00:37:19,619 --> 00:37:20,800
I need those pups.

704
00:37:21,059 --> 00:37:21,940
Don't even think about it.

705
00:37:25,780 --> 00:37:28,760
Can't wait to meet my grandkids and drain their essence.

706
00:37:29,219 --> 00:37:30,880
Leave my kids alone!

707
00:37:31,380 --> 00:37:34,360
If you destroy me, you'll be stuck on that rock forever!

708
00:37:34,699 --> 00:37:35,860
My pups are worth it.

709
00:37:36,469 --> 00:37:41,179
Hmm. I think I just watched someone get condemned to a fate worse than death.

710
00:37:41,599 --> 00:37:47,159
Whoopsie. Jake taps so much of Warren's power, he couldn't even open a portal to get out of there.

711
00:37:47,420 --> 00:37:50,079
He might not be as powerful as Warren at his peak,

712
00:37:50,480 --> 00:37:54,380
but this is, without a doubt, Jake at 100%.

713
00:37:54,380 --> 00:37:58,760
And if you're still saying, Nuh-uh, party animal Jake is peak.

714
00:37:59,420 --> 00:38:02,619
Then I ask not for your forgiveness, for I do not need it.

715
00:38:02,880 --> 00:38:04,659
I thank you for your ears and eyeballs.

716
00:38:05,059 --> 00:38:10,099
If you liked my words, click on all my links and watch every video you see on screen right now.

717
00:38:10,460 --> 00:38:11,800
Or, like, one or two.

718
00:38:12,300 --> 00:38:13,440
Whatever you got time for.

719
00:38:13,780 --> 00:38:18,760
You can even compare how 100% Power Jake compares to some other characters I've already talked about.

720
00:38:19,039 --> 00:38:19,460
Till next time!

721
00:38:19,980 --> 00:38:20,199
Later!

